csrc/elementwise/activation.cuh is an exact copy of the pinned upstream file.
The runtime selects ActivationKernel<bf16_t,false>::run_activation_with_rounding
with operation silu, clamp_limit 0 and fast math disabled. Device arithmetic
is unchanged: BF16 SiLU rounding precedes the BF16 multiply; no clipping,
FP8 quantization, filtering, PDL or in-place output is selected.

compat/sgl_kernel/tensor.h and include/sgl_kernel/* are exact copies of the
existing RTP fp4_indexer frozen bundle's PPU toolchain-compatible headers.
That bundle's host device-name lookup, source-location and CUDA architecture
compatibility fixes are retained; these are support code, not a claim that
those headers originated at the activation kernel's pinned revision.
source-manifest.json identifies and hashes every copied runtime file and the
attribution files. The existing RTP JIT loader never imports SGLang Python.

compat/sgl_kernel/utils.h includes the unchanged qualified support header and
adds the exact Error/CHECK_HOST block from the pinned upstream
python/sglang/kernels/jit/include/sgl_kernel/utils.h. Only its surrounding
namespace is adapted from sglang::host to the older support's global host;
an include guard avoids redefining an existing CHECK_HOST. This preserves
the original lazy stream-message construction and PanicError exception on
failed host checks. It resolves parsing of the generic routed entry points
without changing the selected rounded SiLU kernel or its device arithmetic.
